Article 11: Under any of the following circumstances, a citizen, legal person, or other organization may apply for administrative reconsideration in accordance with this Law:
(1) where it is dissatisfied with an administrative penalty decision made by an administrative organ;
(2) where it is dissatisfied with a decision on administrative compulsion measures or administrative compulsion enforcement made by an administrative organ;
(3) where it applies for an administrative license and the administrative organ refuses or fails to respond within the statutory time limit, or is dissatisfied with other decisions made by the administrative organ concerning the administrative license;
(4) where it is dissatisfied with a decision made by an administrative organ confirming the ownership or right to use natural resources;
(5) where it is dissatisfied with a decision on expropriation or requisition and the compensation decision therefor made by an administrative organ;
(6) where it is dissatisfied with a decision on compensation or a decision not to compensate made by an administrative organ;
(7) where it is dissatisfied with a decision made by an administrative organ not to accept an application for work-related injury determination or the conclusion of work-related injury determination;
(8) where it considers that an administrative organ has violated its operational autonomy or rural land contractual management right, or rural land management right;
(9) where it considers that an administrative organ has abused administrative power to exclude or restrict competition;
(10) where it considers that an administrative organ has illegally raised funds, apportioned expenses, or illegally required the performance of other obligations;
(11) where it applies to an administrative organ to perform statutory duties of protecting personal rights, property rights, the right to education, and other lawful rights and interests, and the administrative organ refuses to perform, fails to perform according to law, or fails to respond;
(12) where it applies to an administrative organ for payment of social security such as pensions, social insurance benefits, or minimum living allowances according to law, and the administrative organ fails to pay according to law;
(13) where it considers that an administrative organ has failed to conclude an administrative agreement according to law, failed to perform according to law, failed to perform as agreed, or illegally modified or rescinded an administrative agreement such as a government franchise agreement or a land and house expropriation compensation agreement;
(14) where it considers that an administrative organ has infringed upon its lawful rights and interests in the work of government information disclosure;
(15) where it considers that other administrative acts of an administrative organ have infringed upon its lawful rights and interests.

Article 12: The following matters shall not fall within the scope of administrative reconsideration:
(1) state acts such as national defense and foreign affairs;
(2) administrative regulations, rules, or normative documents such as decisions and orders with general binding force formulated and issued by administrative organs;
(3) decisions of administrative organs on rewards, punishments, appointments, and removals of administrative organ staff;
(4) mediations conducted by administrative organs on civil disputes.

Article 13: Where a citizen, legal person, or other organization considers that the following normative documents on which an administrative organ's administrative act is based are illegal, when applying for administrative reconsideration of the administrative act, it may simultaneously file with the administrative reconsideration organ an application for collateral review of such normative documents:
(1) normative documents of departments of the State Council;
(2) normative documents of local people's governments at or above the county level and their working departments;
(3) normative documents of township and town people's governments;
(4) normative documents of organizations authorized by laws, regulations, or rules.
The normative documents listed in the preceding paragraph shall not include rules. Review of rules shall be handled in accordance with laws and administrative regulations.

Article 23: Under any of the following circumstances, the applicant shall first apply to the administrative reconsideration organ for administrative reconsideration; where he is dissatisfied with the administrative reconsideration decision, he may then file an administrative lawsuit with the People's Court according to law:
(1) where he is dissatisfied with an administrative penalty decision made on the spot;
(2) where he is dissatisfied with a decision made by an administrative organ that infringes upon his ownership or right to use natural resources lawfully obtained;
(3) where he considers that the administrative organ has failed to perform statutory duties as specified in Article 11 of this Law;
(4) where he applies for disclosure of government information and the administrative organ refuses to disclose it;
(5) other circumstances provided by laws and administrative regulations that require first applying to the administrative reconsideration organ for administrative reconsideration.
For the circumstances specified in the preceding paragraph, the administrative organ shall, when making the administrative act, inform the citizen, legal person, or other organization that it shall first apply to the administrative reconsideration organ for administrative reconsideration.

Article 24: Local people's governments at or above the county level shall have jurisdiction over the following administrative reconsideration cases:
(1) those involving dissatisfaction with an administrative act made by a working department of the people's government at the same level;
(2) those involving dissatisfaction with an administrative act made by a people's government at the next lower level;
(3) those involving dissatisfaction with an administrative act made by an agency established according to law by the people's government at the same level;
(4) those involving dissatisfaction with an administrative act made by an organization authorized by laws, regulations, or rules that is managed by the people's government at the same level or its working department.
In addition to the provisions of the preceding paragraph, the people's government of a province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government shall also have jurisdiction over administrative reconsideration cases involving dissatisfaction with administrative acts made by itself.
An agency established according to law by the people's government of a province or autonomous region shall, by reference to the functions and powers of the people's government of a city divided into districts, have jurisdiction over relevant administrative reconsideration cases.
Administrative reconsideration cases involving dissatisfaction with an administrative act made by an office established according to law by a working department of a local people's government at or above the county level in the name of that office in accordance with laws, regulations, or rules shall be under the jurisdiction of the people's government at the same level; among them, those involving dissatisfaction with an administrative act made by an office established by a working department of the people's government of a municipality directly under the Central Government or a city divided into districts according to administrative divisions may also be under the jurisdiction of the people's government at the place where the office is located.

Article 25: Departments of the State Council shall have jurisdiction over the following administrative reconsideration cases:
(1) those involving dissatisfaction with an administrative act made by the department itself;
(2) those involving dissatisfaction with an administrative act made by an office established according to law by the department in the name of that office in accordance with laws, administrative regulations, and departmental rules;
(3) those involving dissatisfaction with an administrative act made by an organization authorized by laws, administrative regulations, or departmental rules that is managed by the department.

Article 30 After receiving an application for administrative reconsideration, the administrative reconsideration authority shall conduct a review within five days. The administrative reconsideration authority shall accept the application if it meets the following requirements:
(1) There is a clear applicant and a respondent that complies with the provisions of this Law;
(2) The applicant has an interest in the administrative act subject to the application for administrative reconsideration;
(3) There are specific requests and grounds for administrative reconsideration;
(4) The application is filed within the statutory time limit for application;
(5) The matter falls within the scope of administrative reconsideration as stipulated by this Law;
(6) The matter falls within the jurisdiction of this authority;
(7) The administrative reconsideration authority has not previously accepted an application for administrative reconsideration filed by the same applicant concerning the same administrative act, and the People's Court has not accepted an administrative action filed by the same applicant concerning the same administrative act.
For an application for administrative reconsideration that does not meet the requirements of the preceding paragraph, the administrative reconsideration authority shall, within the review period, decide not to accept it and state the reasons; if the matter is not within its jurisdiction, it shall also inform the applicant of the administrative reconsideration authority that has jurisdiction in the decision not to accept.
If the review period for the application for administrative reconsideration expires and the administrative reconsideration authority has not made a decision not to accept, the application shall be deemed accepted as of the date of expiration of the review period.

Article 39. Under any of the following circumstances during the period of administrative reconsideration, the administrative reconsideration shall be suspended:
(1) the applicant, a natural person, dies and it is not yet determined whether his or her near relative will participate in the administrative reconsideration;
(2) the applicant, a natural person, loses capacity to participate in the administrative reconsideration and no statutory agent has been appointed to participate;
(3) the applicant, a natural person, is missing;
(4) the applicant, a legal person or other organization, terminates and it is not yet determined who will succeed to its rights and obligations;
(5) the applicant or the respondent cannot participate in the administrative reconsideration due to force majeure or other legitimate reasons;
(6) mediation or conciliation is being conducted in accordance with this Law, and both the applicant and respondent agree to suspend;
(7) the issue of application of law involved in the administrative reconsideration case requires interpretation or confirmation by an authoritative organ;
(8) the hearing of the administrative reconsideration case needs to be based on the outcome of another case, which has not yet been concluded;
(9) there are circumstances provided for in Article 56 or Article 57 of this Law;
(10) other circumstances requiring the suspension of administrative reconsideration.
After the cause for suspension of administrative reconsideration is eliminated, the hearing of the administrative reconsideration case shall be resumed promptly.
When the administrative reconsideration authority suspends or resumes the hearing of an administrative reconsideration case, it shall inform the parties in writing.

Article 41. Under any of the following circumstances during the period of administrative reconsideration, the administrative reconsideration authority shall decide to terminate the administrative reconsideration:
(1) the applicant withdraws the application for administrative reconsideration and the administrative reconsideration organ approves the withdrawal;
(2) the applicant, a natural person, dies, leaving no near relative, or his or her near relative waives the right to administrative reconsideration;
(3) the applicant, a legal person or other organization, terminates, leaving no successor to its rights and obligations, or the successor waives the right to administrative reconsideration;
(4) after the applicant applies for administrative reconsideration against administrative detention or an administrative compulsory measure restricting personal freedom due to dissatisfaction, he or she is subjected to a criminal compulsory measure because the same illegal act is suspected of constituting a crime;
(5) the administrative reconsideration has been suspended for sixty full days in accordance with subparagraphs (1), (2), and (4) of paragraph 1 of Article 39 of this Law, but the cause for suspension has not yet been eliminated.

Article 42. An administrative act shall not be suspended during the period of administrative reconsideration; however, under any of the following circumstances, its enforcement shall be suspended:
(1) the respondent considers that suspension is necessary;
(2) the administrative reconsideration authority considers that suspension is necessary;
(3) the applicant or a third party applies for suspension, and the administrative reconsideration authority considers the request reasonable and decides to suspend enforcement;
(4) other circumstances provided for by laws, regulations, or rules require suspension of enforcement.

Article 43. The evidence in administrative reconsideration includes:
(1) documentary evidence;
(2) physical evidence;
(3) audio-visual materials;
(4) electronic data;
(5) witness testimony;
(6) statements of the parties;
(7) expert opinions;
(8) records of inspection and on-site records.
The above evidence may be used as the basis for ascertaining the facts of an administrative reconsideration case only after it has been verified as truthful by the administrative reconsideration organ.

Article 44. The respondent bears the burden of adducing evidence for the legality and appropriateness of the administrative act it performed.
Under any of the following circumstances, the applicant shall provide evidence:
(1) if the applicant claims that the respondent fails to perform its statutory duties, the applicant shall provide evidence that it once requested the respondent to perform such duties, unless the respondent shall perform the statutory duties ex officio or the applicant cannot provide the evidence for justifiable reasons;
(2) if the applicant makes a claim for administrative compensation, the applicant shall provide evidence of the damage caused by the administrative act, except that if the applicant cannot adduce evidence due to the respondent's fault, the respondent shall bear the burden of adducing evidence;
(3) other circumstances provided for by laws or regulations require the applicant to provide evidence.

Article 52. People's governments at or above the county level shall establish administrative reconsideration committees involving relevant government departments, experts, and scholars, to provide advisory opinions on handling administrative reconsideration cases and to study and propose opinions on major matters and common issues in administrative reconsideration work. Specific measures for the composition and operation of the administrative reconsideration committee shall be formulated by the administrative reconsideration organ of the State Council.
When hearing an administrative reconsideration case involving any of the following circumstances, the administrative reconsideration organ shall request the administrative reconsideration committee to provide advisory opinions:
(1) the case is of major importance, difficult, or complex;
(2) it involves strong professional or technical issues;
(3) the administrative reconsideration case provided for in paragraph 2 of Article 24 of this Law;
(4) the administrative reconsideration organ considers it necessary.
The administrative reconsideration organ shall record the advisory opinions of the administrative reconsideration committee.

Article 53. An administrative reconsideration authority may apply summary procedure when hearing the following administrative reconsideration cases if it finds the facts are clear, the rights and obligations are clearly defined, and the dispute is minor:
(1) the administrative act under reconsideration was performed on the spot;
(2) the administrative act under reconsideration is a warning or criticism circulated in a notice;
(3) the amount involved in the case is less than 3,000 yuan;
(4) the case is a government information disclosure case.
For administrative reconsideration cases other than those provided in the preceding paragraph, if all parties agree to the application of summary procedure, summary procedure may be applied.

Article 63 The administrative reconsideration authority shall decide to modify the administrative act under any of the following circumstances:
(1) The facts are clear, the evidence is conclusive, the applicable basis is correct, and the procedure is lawful, but the content is inappropriate;
(2) The facts are clear, the evidence is conclusive, and the procedure is lawful, but the applicable basis is not correctly applied;
(3) The facts are unclear or the evidence is insufficient, and the administrative reconsideration authority has clarified the facts and evidence.
The administrative reconsideration authority shall not make a modification decision that is more unfavorable to the applicant, unless a third party raises an opposing request.

Article 64 The administrative reconsideration authority shall decide to revoke or partially revoke the administrative act under any of the following circumstances, and may order the respondent to make a new administrative act within a specified time limit:
(1) The main facts are unclear or the evidence is insufficient;
(2) The statutory procedure is violated;
(3) The applicable basis is illegal;
(4) The authority is exceeded or abused.
If the administrative reconsideration authority orders the respondent to make a new administrative act, the respondent shall not make an administrative act that is identical or substantially identical to the administrative act subject to the application for administrative reconsideration based on the same facts and reasons, unless the administrative reconsideration authority decides to revoke or partially revoke the act on the ground of violation of statutory procedure.

Article 65 Where an administrative act falls under any of the following circumstances, the administrative reconsideration organ shall not revoke the administrative act but shall confirm that the administrative act is illegal:
(1) It shall be revoked according to law, but revocation would cause major damage to national interests or public interests;
(2) The procedure is slightly illegal, but it does not have a material impact on the applicant's rights.
Where an administrative act falls under any of the following circumstances and does not need to be revoked or ordered to be performed, the administrative reconsideration organ shall confirm that the administrative act is illegal:
(1) The administrative act is illegal but has no revocable content;
(2) The respondent has changed the original illegal administrative act, and the applicant still requests revocation or confirmation of the illegality of the administrative act;
(3) The respondent fails to perform or delays the performance of statutory duties, and ordering performance is meaningless.

Article 78 If the applicant or a third party neither institutes a lawsuit within the time limit nor performs the administrative reconsideration decision document or mediation agreement, or fails to perform the final administrative reconsideration decision, the following provisions shall apply respectively:
(1) For an administrative reconsideration decision document that upholds an administrative act, the administrative organ that made the administrative act shall enforce it according to law, or apply to the People's Court for compulsory enforcement;
(2) For an administrative reconsideration decision document that modifies an administrative act, the administrative reconsideration organ shall enforce it according to law, or apply to the People's Court for compulsory enforcement;
(3) For an administrative reconsideration mediation agreement, the administrative reconsideration organ shall enforce it according to law, or apply to the People's Court for compulsory enforcement.
